course: dictionary
lesson: 12315
title: Meet the correspondent
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A correspondent is a person who sends news or letters from one place to another. The words around it give you clues. «Our correspondent in Paris says the museum will reopen next week.» Someone in Paris is sending news back, so a correspondent is a reporter.
explain: A correspondent can also be someone who writes letters to another person regularly. «Maya and her pen-pal are correspondents, and they write to each other every month.» Two people who write to each other are correspondents, even if they never meet.
explain: In formal writing, a correspondent can be a bank that does business for another bank in a different country. You will meet this sense less often. When you are not sure which meaning fits, try the swap test: put «reporter» or «letter writer» into the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Correspondent means a person who sends news or letters from one place to another.
fact: «A foreign correspondent» is a reporter who sends news from another country.
fact: «A war correspondent» reports news from places where there is fighting.
fact: Two people who write to each other regularly are correspondents too.
fact: In banking, a correspondent is a bank that does business for another bank in a different country.
exercise: «Our correspondent in Paris says the museum will reopen next week.» What is a correspondent in this sentence? | *A reporter sending news from Paris | A museum guide | A tourist taking photos of the museum | A French teacher
exercise: «Maya and her pen-pal are correspondents; they write letters every month.» What does correspondents mean here? | Two people who run a shop together | People who fight in a war | People who sing in a choir | *People who write to each other regularly
exercise: «She works as a sports correspondent for the radio.» What does a sports correspondent do? | Sells sports clothes in a shop | Plays football for a team | *Reports news about sport | Teaches swimming at school
test: «The war correspondent sent reports from the front line every night.» What is the main job of the war correspondent in this sentence? | A painter of pictures of the sea | A cook who makes meals for soldiers | *To report news from the fighting | A bus driver on a long route
test: «Grandma and I are correspondents, and I post her a letter every Friday.» What does correspondents suggest about Grandma and the writer? | They never speak to each other | They live in the same house | They are both reporters on the news | *They send letters to each other
exam: «The bank in London is a correspondent of a bank in Tokyo, so they do business for each other.» What does correspondent mean in this sentence? | A school teacher | A person who writes letters to a friend | *A bank that does business for another bank in a different country | A reporter writing news
